        "required_age": 0,
        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >VERDURE is an odd generator of plants and trees! It is a creative sandbox where you can trim branches and experiment with growth controls.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While there is a tutorial with a few objectives to get you started, VERDURE is primarily for open-ended plant design. Whether shaping a small bonsai tree, letting maple branches sprawl freely, or exploring how different settings affect them, you're the artist! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each plant is generated from a unique seed that can be customized through a wide range of parameters, including trunk thickness, branch curvature, foliage shape and distribution, and color palettes. The original soundtrack, retro visuals and little hands-on growth interactions (like feeding a UFO to grow bigger plants) also give the game its distinctive feel. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start from a random seed or design your own through the recipe panel</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Trim and prune branches, or let them grow organically</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Harvest plants that accumulate value over time  and buy collection expansions</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choose combinations of unlocked backgrounds and foregrounds to suit your composition</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Purchase additional tools and pots from the shop</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Preserve your favorite creations across 50+ save slots, with indicative names like ‘Cactus,’ ‘Pine,’ or ‘Sakura’</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >VERDURE can be enjoyed in short, fidget-friendly sessions or over longer periods to gradually expand your collection and refine each plant's design.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >VERDURE is an odd generator of plants and trees! It is a creative sandbox where you can trim branches and experiment with growth controls.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >While there is a tutorial with a few objectives to get you started, VERDURE is primarily for open-ended plant design. Whether shaping a small bonsai tree, letting maple branches sprawl freely, or exploring how different settings affect them, you're the artist! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each plant is generated from a unique seed that can be customized through a wide range of parameters, including trunk thickness, branch curvature, foliage shape and distribution, and color palettes. The original soundtrack, retro visuals and little hands-on growth interactions (like feeding a UFO to grow bigger plants) also give the game its distinctive feel. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start from a random seed or design your own through the recipe panel</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Trim and prune branches, or let them grow organically</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Harvest plants that accumulate value over time  and buy collection expansions</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choose combinations of unlocked backgrounds and foregrounds to suit your composition</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Purchase additional tools and pots from the shop</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Preserve your favorite creations across 50+ save slots, with indicative names like ‘Cactus,’ ‘Pine,’ or ‘Sakura’</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >VERDURE can be enjoyed in short, fidget-friendly sessions or over longer periods to gradually expand your collection and refine each plant's design.</p>",
        "short_description": "Shape nature your way in a surreal playground of infinite plants and trees. Tweak their recipes, prune or let them flourish, and save your best creations into an ever growing collection.",
